       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT effects, GI effects, and seizures. They also have no added evidence of benefit. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function) would justify going above the maximum.\n\nPlease check a few things:\n- **Dose:** Did you mean 40 mg or 100 mg, or is this a typo? Typical dosing is 50 mg daily, titrated up to a maximum of 200 mg.\n- **Indication:** The usual starting doses are 25\u201350 mg for anxiety, PTSD, and depression, and 50 mg for OCD, with titration from there.\n- **Attending or pharmacist:** If a dose above the maximum is truly intended, for example in a specialist-directed case, confirm it with your attending or pharmacist first. It will probably need a documented rationale.\n\nOnce you give me the corrected dose, or confirm that your attending approved 400 mg, I'll enter the order right away. I can add a note to the order with the rationale if you want."
